.TH LOD.QOS_THRESHOLD_RR 4 2026-09-29 Lustre "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
lod.qos_threshold_rr, lod.mdt_qos_threshold_rr \- free space balance threshold
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.BI "lctl get_param lod." FSNAME "*.qos_threshold_rr"
.SY
.BI "lctl set_param lod." FSNAME "*.qos_threshold_rr=" PERCENT
.SY
.BI "lctl get_param lod." FSNAME "*.mdt_qos_threshold_rr"
.SY
.BI "lctl set_param lod." FSNAME "*.mdt_qos_threshold_rr=" PERCENT
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Perms
.br
.BR 644 " | " -rw-r--r--
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Per-MDT
.TP
.B Config
.br
Always present on MDS nodes
.TP
.B Default
.br
.RB lod.*.qos_threshold_rr= 17%
.br
.RB lod.*.mdt_qos_threshold_rr= 5%
.TP
.B Valid Range
.br
.RB lod.*.qos_threshold_rr= 0%
.br
.RB lod.*.qos_threshold_rr= 100%
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qos_threshold_rr
decides whether the MDS allocates the objects of new files on OSTs in
round-robin order, or by the free space of the OSTs (QoS allocation).
.B mdt_qos_threshold_rr
does the same for the stripes of new striped directories on MDTs, where
the free inodes of each MDT are taken into account as well.
.PP
While the free space of the most full target is within
.I PERCENT
of the free space of the least full one, the targets are considered
balanced and are used in round-robin order.
When the difference is larger, the targets are used by free space as
described in
.BR lod.qos_prio_free (4),
so that fuller targets are used less often until they are balanced
again.
.PP
With
.I PERCENT
set to 100% the targets are always used in round-robin order, and with
0% they are always used by free space.
The
.B %
sign is optional when setting the value, which is kept in 1/256 steps
and shown rounded up to the next whole percent.
.PP
The free space of the targets is refreshed at the interval given by
.BR lod.qos_maxage (4).
.SH EXAMPLES
Allocate OST objects by free space whenever the OSTs differ by more than
5% on all MDTs of the
.B testfs
filesystem:
.EX
.RB "mds# " "lctl set_param lod.testfs-*.qos_threshold_rr=5"
.EE
.PP
Always allocate OST objects in round-robin order:
.EX
.RB "mds# " "lctl set_param lod.testfs-*.qos_threshold_rr=100"
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
.B qos_threshold_rr
is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.4.0, and
.B mdt_qos_threshold_rr
since release 2.13.0.
Before that it was
.BR lov.qos_threshold_rr ,
since release 2.0.0.
